      "body": "# PANDA Token Validation API\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Token Validation API is used by SDKs to validate access tokens during the `panda init` process. This implements a one-time activation model where each token can only be validated once.\n\n## Endpoint\n\n```\nPOST /v1/tokens/validate\n```\n\n**Base URLs:**\n- Production: `https://csirt.jatimprov.go.id/panda/api/v1/tokens/validate`\n- Local: `http://localhost:8088/v1/tokens/validate`\n\n**Authentication:** Not required (public endpoint, rate-limited by IP)\n\n---\n\n## Request\n\n### Headers\n\n```\nContent-Type: application/json\n```\n\n### Body\n\n```json\n{\n  \"token\": \"panda_live_76d08573d453cdbdb4bf5704d13f8f54d57cd3c47c9b4be2\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type   | Required | Description           |\n|-------|--------|----------|-----------------------|\n| token | string | Yes      | The plaintext access token |\n\n---\n\n## Response\n\n### Success Response (200 OK)\n\nWhen the token is valid and unused:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"valid\": true,\n  \"applicationId\": \"app_1234567890\",\n  \"organizationId\": \"org_1234567890\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field           | Type    | Description                           |\n|-----------------|---------|---------------------------------------|\n| valid           | boolean | `true` when token is valid            |\n| applicationId   | string  | The application ID (only when valid)  |\n| organizationId  | string  | The organization ID (only when valid)  |\n\n### Invalid Response (200 OK)\n\nWhen the token is invalid, revoked, or already activated:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"valid\": false,\n  \"reason\": \"invalid\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field  | Type   | Description                                                    |\n|--------|--------|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n| valid  | boolean | `false` when token is invalid                                 |\n| reason | string  | One of: `invalid`, `revoked`, `already_activated`              |\n\n---\n\n## Reason Values\n\n| Value               | Description                                      |\n|---------------------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| `invalid`           | Token not found or malformed                      |\n| `revoked`           | Token has been revoked by the portal admin       |\n| `already_activated` | Token was already used (one-time activation)      |\n\n---\n\n## Token Lifecycle\n\n```\nunused → activated (first successful validation)\n         ↓\n       cannot be reused\n         \nunused → revoked (by admin)\n         ↓\n       validation fails with \"revoked\"\n```\n\n**Important:** Once a token transitions from `unused` to `activated`, it cannot be used again. Any subsequent validation attempts will return `reason: \"already_activated\"`.\n\n---\n\n## Example Usage\n\n### cURL\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://csirt.jatimprov.go.id/panda/api/v1/tokens/validate \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"token\":\"panda_live_76d08573d453cdbdb4bf5704d13f8f54d57cd3c47c9b4be2\"}'\n```\n\n### JavaScript/TypeScript\n\n```typescript\nasync function validateToken(token: string) {\n  const response = await fetch('https://csirt.jatimprov.go.id/panda/api/v1/tokens/validate', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ token })\n  });\n  \n  const result = await response.json();\n  \n  if (result.valid) {\n    console.log('Application ID:', result.applicationId);\n    console.log('Organization ID:', result.organizationId);\n  } else {\n    console.error('Token validation failed:', result.reason);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Go\n\n```go\ntype ValidateTokenRequest struct {\n    Token string `json:\"token\"`\n}\n\ntype ValidateTokenResponse struct {\n    Valid          bool   `json:\"valid\"`\n    ApplicationID  string `json:\"applicationId,omitempty\"`\n    OrganizationID string `json:\"organizationId,omitempty\"`\n    Reason         string `json:\"reason,omitempty\"`\n}\n\nfunc validateToken(token string) (*ValidateTokenResponse, error) {\n    body, _ := json.Marshal(ValidateTokenRequest{Token: token})\n    \n    resp, err := http.Post(\n        \"https://csirt.jatimprov.go.id/panda/api/v1/tokens/validate\",\n        \"application/json\",\n        bytes.NewReader(body),\n    )\n    if err != nil {\n        return nil, err\n    }\n    defer resp.Body.Close()\n    \n    var result ValidateTokenResponse\n    json.NewDecoder(resp.Body).Decode(&result)\n    return &result, nil\n}\n```\n\n### PHP\n\n```php\nfunction validateToken(string $token): array {\n    $ch = curl_init('https://csirt.jatimprov.go.id/panda/api/v1/tokens/validate');\n    \n    curl_setopt_array($ch, [\n        CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER => true,\n        CURLOPT_POST => true,\n        CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER => ['Content-Type: application/json'],\n        CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS => json_encode(['token' => $token]),\n    ]);\n    \n    $response = curl_exec($ch);\n    curl_close($ch);\n    \n    return json_decode($response, true);\n}\n\n// Usage\n$result = validateToken('panda_live_76d08573d453cdbdb4bf5704d13f8f54d57cd3c47c9b4be2');\n\nif ($result['valid']) {\n    echo \"Application ID: \" . $result['applicationId'] . \"\\n\";\n    echo \"Organization ID: \" . $result['organizationId'] . \"\\n\";\n} else {\n    echo \"Validation failed: \" . $result['reason'] . \"\\n\";\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Status | Body                          | Description                                |\n|--------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|\n| 400    | `{\"error\":\"token is required\"}` | Missing or empty token field             |\n| 200    | `{\"valid\":false, \"reason\":\"...\"}` | Token validation failed (any reason)    |\n\n**Note:** Internal server errors are intentionally masked as invalid tokens to prevent information leakage about the backend system.\n\n---\n\n## Security Considerations\n\n1. **Token storage:** The SDK should hash the token locally after validation and never store the plaintext\n2. **Transport:** Always use HTTPS in production\n3. **Rate limiting:** The endpoint is rate-limited by IP to prevent abuse\n4. **One-time use:** Each token can only be validated once; handle the `already_activated` case gracefully\n\n---\n\n## Token Format (Reference)\n\nTokens follow this pattern:\n```\npanda_(demo|live)_[48 hex characters]\n```\n\nExample: `panda_live_76d08573d453cdbdb4bf5704d13f8f54d57cd3c47c9b4be2`\n\n---\n\n## Related Endpoints\n\n| Endpoint                    | Method | Description                     |\n|-----------------------------|--------|---------------------------------|\n| `/v1/applications/{id}/tokens` | POST | Issue a new token (authenticated) |\n| `/v1/applications/{id}/tokens` | GET  | List tokens for an application   |\n| `/v1/applications/{id}/tokens/{tokenId}` | DELETE | Revoke a token              |\n",
      "source": {
        "repo": "panda-docs",
        "path": "key-validation-feature.md",
        "commit": "unknown"
      }
